import tmp.sheaf.xif.paper.S2502FiniteLevelODiamondActual
import tmp.sheaf.xif.paper.S2500CategoricalOtriangleActual
import tmp.sheaf.xif.paper.S2501UniversalCoverSystemActual

/-!
# S2504: finite-level `O^▷ ⊆ O^◃` submonoid and pro-generator data

(Here "S2501" is `S2501UniversalCoverSystemActual`, the actual
finite-Galois inverse system; `S2501MatrixPairEquivActual` is an
unrelated cycle-type file and is not imported.)

## What the paper asks for

IUT II, Definition 4.9, (viii) uses, at each bad place and each finite level of
the universal covering, the monoid `O^▷(−) ⊆ O^◃(−)`, each `O^▷(−)`
being generated by one element and abstractly isomorphic to `ℕ`.  In the
finite-level carrier of S2502 this is
`S2502ODiamond p L = (S2502IntegralClosure p L)⁰`, the nonzero
elements of the integral closure of the `p`-adic valuation ring in the
finite Galois intermediate field `L`.

## What this file defines

* `S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L g` (section 1): the submonoid of
  `S2502ODiamond p L` generated by the single element `g`, i.e.
  `Submonoid.powers g`, with its membership characterization, its
  universal property, its image under a monoid hom, and the fact that the
  trivial generator `1` generates `⊥` (so `1` is not the paper's
  `O^▷`-generator).
* `S2504OTriangleLevelData p L` (section 2): **the paper's finite-level
  `O^▷` generator datum**: a generator that is not an integral unit, whose
  natural powers are distinct (`O^▷ ≅ ℕ`), and whose generated submonoid
  is proper.  No inhabitant is constructed here.
* `S2504LevelTransition p h` (section 3): the monoid-level transition
  on the finite-level `O^◃` carriers over an S2501 index morphism, with
  its compatibility with the actual S2501 field transition.  The reflexive
  transition is constructed; the general one is not constructed from
  S2501/S2502 alone.
* `S2504ProGeneratorData p` (section 4): the full pro-generator datum
  over the actual finite-Galois inverse system: one level datum at every
  finite level, a monoid transition over every index morphism compatible with
  the actual field transition, the identity-transition law, and the generator
  at the finer level mapping to the generator at the coarser level.  Under this
  datum the generated `O^▷` submonoids are proved to be mapped onto each
  other (S2504ProGeneratorData_map_submonoid), and the underlying family of
  `O^◃` carriers is assembled into an actual `S2500ProSystem`
  (S2504ProGeneratorData_proSystem).  No inhabitant is constructed here.

## Exact missing (no fake)

The paper's actual generator is a uniformizer of `L` (a non-unit integral
element whose powers exhaust `O^▷ ≅ ℕ`).  Neither S2502's carrier nor
S2501's inverse system provides: a valuation or uniformizer of the finite
field `L`; a proof that a given nonzero integral element is not a unit;
a proof that its natural powers are distinct; a proof that its generated
submonoid is proper in `O^◃`; or the integrality transfer giving a monoid
hom `S2502ODiamond p M →* S2502ODiamond p L` over an index morphism.
These are recorded exactly as fields of `S2504OTriangleLevelData` and
`S2504ProGeneratorData`, with no inhabitant and no axiom.  The local
generator `localOFieldFive` of S2032 is a term of the different carrier
`LocalOFieldIntegral 5`, not of `S2502ODiamond p L`; no transport of that
local uniformizer to a general finite Galois `L` (and no proof of the
required properties there) is available, so it does not inhabit the
structures here.

The file does not identify `O^▷` with the whole monoid `O^◃`: the level
datum explicitly requires properness, and S2504NoTopLevelData records that no
datum has `⊤` as its generated submonoid.  It also does not install the
trivial generator `1`: S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_one proves it generates `⊥`,
and S2504NoTrivialLevelData records that no datum has `⊥` as its
generated submonoid.  No `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `True`/`PUnit` gate,
arbitrary element, or assumption-only abbreviation is used.
-/

noncomputable section
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.checkUnivs false
set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000

open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2500CategoricalOtriangleActual
open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2501UniversalCoverSystemActual
open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2502FiniteLevelODiamondActual
open scoped nonZeroDivisors

namespace LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2504OTriangleGeneratorsActual

/-! ## 1. The submonoid of `O^◃(L)` generated by one element -/

/-- The submonoid of the finite-level carrier `O^◃(L)` generated by the
single element `g`.  By definition this is `Submonoid.powers g`:
the candidate `O^▷(L) ⊆ O^◃(L)` of IUT II, Definition 4.9, (viii). -/
noncomputable abbrev S2504GeneratedSubmonoid
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (L : S2501Index p) (g : S2502ODiamond p L.1) :
    Submonoid (S2502ODiamond p L.1) :=
  Submonoid.powers g

/-- Membership in the generated submonoid is exactly being a natural power of
the generator. -/
theorem S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_mem_iff
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (L : S2501Index p) (g x : S2502ODiamond p L.1) :
    x ∈ S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L g ↔ ∃ n : ℕ, g ^ n = x :=
  Submonoid.mem_powers_iff x g

/-- The underlying set of the generated submonoid is the range of the natural
power map of the generator. -/
theorem S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_coe
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (L : S2501Index p) (g : S2502ODiamond p L.1) :
    (S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L g : Set (S2502ODiamond p L.1)) =
      Set.range fun n : ℕ => g ^ n :=
  Submonoid.coe_powers g

/-- The generator belongs to the submonoid it generates. -/
theorem S2504Generator_mem
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (L : S2501Index p) (g : S2502ODiamond p L.1) :
    g ∈ S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L g :=
  Submonoid.mem_powers g

/-- The generated submonoid is the closure of the singleton generator: the
paper's "generated by one element". -/
theorem S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_eq_closure
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (L : S2501Index p) (g : S2502ODiamond p L.1) :
    S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L g =
      Submonoid.closure ({g} : Set (S2502ODiamond p L.1)) :=
  Submonoid.powers_eq_closure g

/-- Universal property: the generated submonoid is contained in a submonoid
`T` if and only if the generator is in `T`. -/
theorem S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_le_iff
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (L : S2501Index p) {g : S2502ODiamond p L.1}
    (T : Submonoid (S2502ODiamond p L.1)) :
    S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L g ≤ T ↔ g ∈ T :=
  Submonoid.powers_le

/-- The trivial generator `1` generates the trivial submonoid `⊥`; this is
*not* the paper's `O^▷`, and no level datum below can have `⊥` as its
submonoid. -/
theorem S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_one
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] (L : S2501Index p) :
    S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L (1 : S2502ODiamond p L.1) = ⊥ :=
  Submonoid.powers_one

/-- The image of the generated submonoid under a monoid hom is the submonoid
generated by the image of the generator. -/
theorem S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_map
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    {L M : S2501Index p}
    (f : S2502ODiamond p L.1 →* S2502ODiamond p M.1)
    (g : S2502ODiamond p L.1) :
    (S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L g).map f =
      S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p M (f g) :=
  Submonoid.map_powers f g

/-! ## 2. The finite-level `O^▷` generator datum -/

/-- **The paper's finite-level `O^▷` generator datum.**  At a finite Galois
level `L` (an actual finite-dimensional Galois intermediate field, S2501),
the paper's `O^▷(L) ⊆ O^◃(L)` is generated by one element and is
abstractly `ℕ`.  The fields record exactly that datum:

* `generator` is the generator, an actual element of
  `S2502ODiamond p L = O^◃(L)`;
* `generator_not_unit` says that it is not an integral unit (the
  paper's `O^▷` is not carried by the unit group `O^×` and is not
  trivial);
* `powers_injective` says that its natural powers are distinct, so
  `Submonoid.powers generator ≅ ℕ`;
* `submonoid_ne_top` says that the generated submonoid is proper in
  `O^◃(L)`, excluding the fake identification `O^▷ = O^◃`.

No inhabitant of this structure is constructed in this file. -/
structure S2504OTriangleLevelData
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] (L : S2501Index p) where
  /-- The `O^▷`-generator, as an actual element of `O^◃(L)`. -/
  generator : S2502ODiamond p L.1
  /-- The generator is not an integral unit. -/
  generator_not_unit : ¬ IsUnit generator
  /-- The natural powers of the generator are distinct. -/
  powers_injective : Function.Injective fun n : ℕ => generator ^ n
  /-- The generated submonoid is a proper submonoid of `O^◃(L)`. -/
  submonoid_ne_top : Submonoid.powers generator ≠ ⊤

/-- The finite-level `O^▷ ⊆ O^◃`: the submonoid generated by the
datum's generator. -/
noncomputable abbrev S2504LevelSubmonoid
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] {L : S2501Index p}
    (D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L) :
    Submonoid (S2502ODiamond p L.1) :=
  S2504GeneratedSubmonoid p L D.generator

/-- The generator of the datum lies in `O^▷`. -/
theorem S2504LevelSubmonoid_generator_mem
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] {L : S2501Index p}
    (D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L) :
    D.generator ∈ S2504LevelSubmonoid p D :=
  S2504Generator_mem p L D.generator

/-- Universal property form for the level submonoid. -/
theorem S2504LevelSubmonoid_le_iff
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] {L : S2501Index p}
    (D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L)
    (T : Submonoid (S2502ODiamond p L.1)) :
    S2504LevelSubmonoid p D ≤ T ↔ D.generator ∈ T :=
  S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_le_iff p L T

/-- A generator of the paper's `O^▷` is not `1`: `1` is a unit, while the
generator is required to be a non-unit. -/
theorem S2504LevelData_generator_ne_one
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] {L : S2501Index p}
    (D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L) :
    D.generator ≠ 1 := by
  intro h
  exact D.generator_not_unit (h.symm ▸ isUnit_one)

/-- `O^▷` is not the trivial submonoid. -/
theorem S2504LevelSubmonoid_ne_bot
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] {L : S2501Index p}
    (D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L) :
    S2504LevelSubmonoid p D ≠ ⊥ := by
  intro hbot
  have hmem : D.generator ∈ (⊥ : Submonoid (S2502ODiamond p L.1)) := by
    rw [← hbot]
    exact S2504LevelSubmonoid_generator_mem p D
  exact S2504LevelData_generator_ne_one p D (Submonoid.mem_bot.mp hmem)

/-- `O^▷` is a proper submonoid of `O^◃`, not the whole monoid. -/
theorem S2504LevelSubmonoid_ne_top
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] {L : S2501Index p}
    (D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L) :
    S2504LevelSubmonoid p D ≠ ⊤ :=
  D.submonoid_ne_top

/-- `O^▷` is abstractly isomorphic to `ℕ`, as the paper requires for
`O^▷(−)` (IUT II, Definition 4.9, (viii)). -/
noncomputable def S2504LevelSubmonoid_powLogEquiv
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] {L : S2501Index p}
    (D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L) :
    Multiplicative ℕ ≃* S2504LevelSubmonoid p D := by
  classical
  exact Submonoid.powLogEquiv D.powers_injective

/-- No level datum has the trivial submonoid as its `O^▷`: the trivial
generator `1` is excluded by the datum. -/
theorem S2504NoTrivialLevelData
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] (L : S2501Index p) :
    ¬ ∃ D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L, S2504LevelSubmonoid p D = ⊥ := by
  rintro ⟨D, hbot⟩
  exact S2504LevelSubmonoid_ne_bot p D hbot

/-- No level datum has the whole monoid `O^◃` as its `O^▷`: the fake
identification `O^▷ = O^◃` is excluded by the datum. -/
theorem S2504NoTopLevelData
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] (L : S2501Index p) :
    ¬ ∃ D : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L, S2504LevelSubmonoid p D = ⊤ := by
  rintro ⟨D, htop⟩
  exact S2504LevelSubmonoid_ne_top p D htop

/-! ## 3. Monoid-level transitions between finite levels -/

/-- **Monoid-level transition over an S2501 index morphism.**  S2501 provides
only the actual field map `S2501Transition p h : M.1 → L.1`; the induced
hom on the nonzero integral carriers is additional data.  This structure
records exactly that datum together with its compatibility with the actual
field transition. -/
structure S2504LevelTransition
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    {L M : S2501Index p} (h : S2501Le p L M) where
  /-- The monoid transition `O^◃(M) →* O^◃(L)`. -/
  transition : S2502ODiamond p M.1 →* S2502ODiamond p L.1
  /-- The monoid transition is compatible with the S2501 field transition. -/
  transition_compat : ∀ y : S2502ODiamond p M.1,
    ((transition y : S2502IntegralClosure p L.1) : L.1) =
      S2501Transition p h ((y : S2502IntegralClosure p M.1) : M.1)

/-- The identity transition over the reflexive index morphism is compatible
with the actual field transition. -/
noncomputable def S2504LevelTransition_refl
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] (L : S2501Index p) :
    S2504LevelTransition p (S2501Le_refl p L) where
  transition := MonoidHom.id (S2502ODiamond p L.1)
  transition_compat := by
    intro y
    apply Subtype.ext
    rfl

/-- **Transition compatibility of the generated `O^▷`.**  If a monoid
transition sends the level-`M` generator to the level-`L` generator, then
it maps the generated submonoid at `M` onto the generated submonoid at
`L`. -/
theorem S2504LevelSubmonoid_map
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    {L M : S2501Index p} {h : S2501Le p L M}
    (T : S2504LevelTransition p h)
    (DM : S2504OTriangleLevelData p M) (DL : S2504OTriangleLevelData p L)
    (hgen : T.transition DM.generator = DL.generator) :
    (S2504LevelSubmonoid p DM).map T.transition = S2504LevelSubmonoid p DL := by
  show (Submonoid.powers DM.generator).map T.transition =
    Submonoid.powers DL.generator
  rw [Submonoid.map_powers, hgen]

/-! ## 4. The pro-generator datum over the actual S2501 inverse system -/

/-- **The paper's `O^▷` pro-generator datum** over the actual
finite-Galois inverse system `S2501Index`.  It bundles:

* the finite-level generator datum `S2504OTriangleLevelData` at every
  finite Galois level;
* a monoid transition on `O^◃` over every S2501 index morphism,
  compatible with the actual field transition;
* the identity-transition law at reflexive index morphisms;
* the generator compatibility: the transition over `h : S2501Le p L M`
  sends the generator at the finer level `M` to the generator at the
  coarser level `L` (the `generator_compat` condition of S2500's
  `S2500UniversalCoverRequired`, at the actual finite levels).

No inhabitant of this structure is constructed in this file. -/
structure S2504ProGeneratorData
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] where
  /-- The finite-level `O^▷` generator datum at each finite Galois level. -/
  levelData : ∀ L : S2501Index p, S2504OTriangleLevelData p L
  /-- The monoid transition over each S2501 index morphism, compatible with
  the actual S2501 field transition. -/
  levelTransition : ∀ {L M : S2501Index p} (h : S2501Le p L M),
    S2504LevelTransition p h
  /-- The transition over a reflexive index morphism is the identity. -/
  levelTransition_refl : ∀ (L : S2501Index p) (x : S2502ODiamond p L.1),
    (levelTransition (S2501Le_refl p L)).transition x = x
  /-- The transition sends the finer generator to the coarser generator. -/
  maps_generator : ∀ {L M : S2501Index p} (h : S2501Le p L M),
    (levelTransition h).transition (levelData M).generator =
      (levelData L).generator

/-- **The pro-generator transition compatibility.**  Under the paper's
pro-generator datum, the transition over any S2501 index morphism maps the
generated `O^▷` at the finer level onto the generated `O^▷` at the
coarser level. -/
theorem S2504ProGeneratorData_map_submonoid
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (D : S2504ProGeneratorData p)
    {L M : S2501Index p} (h : S2501Le p L M) :
    (S2504LevelSubmonoid p (D.levelData M)).map
        (D.levelTransition h).transition =
      S2504LevelSubmonoid p (D.levelData L) :=
  S2504LevelSubmonoid_map p (D.levelTransition h) (D.levelData M)
    (D.levelData L) (D.maps_generator h)

/-- Each finite level of the paper's pro-generator datum has `O^▷ ≅ ℕ`. -/
theorem S2504ProGeneratorData_level_powLogEquiv
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (D : S2504ProGeneratorData p) (L : S2501Index p) :
    Nonempty (Multiplicative ℕ ≃* S2504LevelSubmonoid p (D.levelData L)) :=
  ⟨S2504LevelSubmonoid_powLogEquiv p (D.levelData L)⟩

/-- The actual family of finite-level `O^◃` monoids underlying the
pro-generator datum, assembled as an `S2500ProSystem`.  Its index
category is the actual S2501 finite-Galois system and its objects are the
actual nonzero integral carriers `S2502ODiamond p L`.  (The remaining
field of S2500's `S2500UniversalCoverRequired`, the map
`toODiamond` into the ambient local integral monoid, is not constructed here:
it would need the integrality transfer from `S2502IntegralClosure p L` to
`LocalAlgebraicIntegerRing p`.) -/
noncomputable def S2504ProGeneratorData_proSystem
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] (D : S2504ProGeneratorData p) :
    S2500ProSystem where
  Index := S2501Index p
  le := S2501Le p
  le_refl := S2501Le_refl p
  le_trans := fun hLM hMN => S2501Le_trans p hLM hMN
  obj := fun L => S2502ODiamond p L.1
  transition := fun {L M} h x => (D.levelTransition h).transition x
  transition_refl := fun L x => D.levelTransition_refl L x

/-! ## 5. Exact missing paper generator data (recorded, not inhabited) -/

/-- Exact missing paper datum at a finite Galois level: a genuine `O^▷`
generator in `O^◃(L)`.  This is a transparent type synonym for
`S2504OTriangleLevelData`; no inhabitant is asserted, and the trivial
generator `1` is not one (it generates `⊥`). -/
abbrev S2504PaperGeneratorRequired
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] (L : S2501Index p) : Type :=
  S2504OTriangleLevelData p L

/-- Exact missing paper pro-generator datum over the actual S2501 inverse
system.  No inhabitant is asserted. -/
abbrev S2504PaperProGeneratorRequired
    (p : Nat) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] : Type :=
  S2504ProGeneratorData p

/-
The exact missing pieces recorded by the structures above are:

1. an element `g : S2502ODiamond p L` that is a uniformizer of the finite
   extension `L / ℚ_[p]`; no valuation, uniformizer, or ramification
   interface for the intermediate field `L` is available in
   S2501/S2502;
2. a proof that `g` is not a unit of the integral closure;
3. a proof that `n ↦ g ^ n` is injective (`O^▷ ≅ ℕ`);
4. a proof that the generated submonoid is proper in `O^◃`;
5. for every `h : S2501Le p L M`, a monoid hom
   `S2502ODiamond p M →* S2502ODiamond p L` compatible with
   `S2501Transition p h`; the field inclusion does induce one
   mathematically, but the integrality transfer is not constructed here;
6. the identity-transition law, and the generator compatibility over every
   `S2501Le`.

No inhabitant of `S2504OTriangleLevelData` or `S2504ProGeneratorData` is
constructed in this file.  In particular the file does not claim that the
paper's generator data exists in the current development.
-/

#check S2504GeneratedSubmonoid
#check S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_one
#check S2504OTriangleLevelData
#check S2504LevelTransition
#check S2504LevelTransition_refl
#check S2504LevelSubmonoid_powLogEquiv
#check S2504ProGeneratorData
#check S2504ProGeneratorData_map_submonoid
#check S2504ProGeneratorData_proSystem
#check S2504PaperGeneratorRequired
#check S2504PaperProGeneratorRequired

#print axioms S2504GeneratedSubmonoid_map
#print axioms S2504LevelSubmonoid_powLogEquiv
#print axioms S2504ProGeneratorData_map_submonoid

end LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2504OTriangleGeneratorsActual
